  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Traditional chumbe sash woven by a member of the Camentsá people in Colombia. Features semasiographic writing.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="590" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">RBC copy: Housed with 2 CDs. CDs are recordings of 2 events held in Spanish: Poetry Reading and Oraliture, Hugo Jamioy Juagibioy, Camëntsá Nation, April 14, 2015, Fedex Global Education Center, UNC, Chapel Hill; and Chumbe Weaving &amp; Storytelling, Mamá Pastora Juajibioy, Camëntsá Nation, April 15, 2015, Sloane Art Library, UNC, Chapel Hill. Recordings include information about how the chumbe is made, and what stories it encodes. Event poster removed to bibliographic file. Use of audio or visual material may require production of listening or viewing copies before use.  Contact wilsonlibrary@unc.edu before visiting reading room for more information.</subfield>
  </datafield>
